{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"fef5ab8f-c9c5-45aa-9619-429c5a994111\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Passage 1: Dashboards and Decisions\\n\\nPublic dashboards can make complex information easier to examine, but visibility does not automatically produce understanding. A chart may be accurate and still mislead if its scale hides variation or if a headline ignores uncertainty. Good dashboards therefore explain where data came from, when they were updated and what they cannot show. They also allow users to compare like with like. The aim is not to remove judgement from decision-making; it is to give judgement a clearer foundation.\\n\\nQuestion: Why should a dashboard state when data were updated?\",\"hi\":\"Passage 1: Dashboards and Decisions\\n\\nPublic dashboards can make complex information easier to examine, but visibility does not automatically produce understanding. A chart may be accurate and still mislead if its scale hides variation or if a headline ignores uncertainty. Good dashboards therefore explain where data came from, when they were updated and what they cannot show. They also allow users to compare like with like. The aim is not to remove judgement from decision-making; it is to give judgement a clearer foundation.\\n\\nQuestion: Why should a dashboard state when data were updated?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Older data are always legally invalid.\",\"hi\":\"Older data are always legally invalid.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Updates make every comparison unnecessary.\",\"hi\":\"Updates make every comparison unnecessary.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Users need to judge how current the information is.\",\"hi\":\"Users need to judge how current the information is.\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The date determines the colour of the chart.\",\"hi\":\"The date determines the colour of the chart.\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Comprehension Passage\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d9fbfc58-c899-4ece-bf2c-2026854b3d24\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Passage 2: The Value of Urban Wetlands\\n\\nAn urban wetland may look like unused land, especially during a dry season. Yet it can store rainwater, support birds and reduce pressure on drainage systems. Building over such an area may create immediate economic value, but it can also transfer hidden costs to nearby neighbourhoods through greater flood risk. Protecting a wetland does not mean preventing all public access. Paths and viewing areas can be designed carefully, provided that the most sensitive zones remain undisturbed.\\n\\nQuestion: Why might an urban wetland be mistaken for unused land?\",\"hi\":\"Passage 2: The Value of Urban Wetlands\\n\\nAn urban wetland may look like unused land, especially during a dry season. Yet it can store rainwater, support birds and reduce pressure on drainage systems. Building over such an area may create immediate economic value, but it can also transfer hidden costs to nearby neighbourhoods through greater flood risk. Protecting a wetland does not mean preventing all public access. Paths and viewing areas can be designed carefully, provided that the most sensitive zones remain undisturbed.\\n\\nQuestion: Why might an urban wetland be mistaken for unused land?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It contains no plants during any season.\",\"hi\":\"It contains no plants during any season.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It is always closed to the public.\",\"hi\":\"It is always closed to the public.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Its ecological functions may not be obvious, especially when it is dry.\",\"hi\":\"Its ecological functions may not be obvious, especially when it is dry.\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It has already been prepared for construction.\",\"hi\":\"It has already been prepared for construction.\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Comprehension Passage\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d6e2e0a3-f0c4-4335-9a15-7f3cc55deff7\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Passage 4: Communicating Scientific Uncertainty\\n\\nUncertainty in a scientific estimate is not evidence that the estimate is useless. It describes the range within which available evidence supports a conclusion. Problems arise when uncertainty is either hidden or exaggerated. Hiding it creates false confidence; exaggerating it can make well-supported findings appear arbitrary. Clear communication states what is known, what remains uncertain and whether new evidence is likely to change the conclusion substantially.\\n\\nQuestion: Which statement best reflects the passage?\",\"hi\":\"Passage 4: Communicating Scientific Uncertainty\\n\\nUncertainty in a scientific estimate is not evidence that the estimate is useless. It describes the range within which available evidence supports a conclusion. Problems arise when uncertainty is either hidden or exaggerated. Hiding it creates false confidence; exaggerating it can make well-supported findings appear arbitrary. Clear communication states what is known, what remains uncertain and whether new evidence is likely to change the conclusion substantially.\\n\\nQuestion: Which statement best reflects the passage?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Any uncertainty makes evidence worthless.\",\"hi\":\"Any uncertainty makes evidence worthless.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Acknowledged uncertainty can strengthen rather than weaken honest communication.\",\"hi\":\"Acknowledged uncertainty can strengthen rather than weaken honest communication.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Scientific estimates should never be revised.\",\"hi\":\"Scientific estimates should never be revised.\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Confidence is preferable to accuracy.\",\"hi\":\"Confidence is preferable to accuracy.\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Comprehension Passage\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c3670324-9a56-4d00-bee5-08c996bcf5ba\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Passage 1: Dashboards and Decisions\\n\\nPublic dashboards can make complex information easier to examine, but visibility does not automatically produce understanding. A chart may be accurate and still mislead if its scale hides variation or if a headline ignores uncertainty. Good dashboards therefore explain where data came from, when they were updated and what they cannot show. They also allow users to compare like with like. The aim is not to remove judgement from decision-making; it is to give judgement a clearer foundation.\\n\\nQuestion: According to the author, data should:\",\"hi\":\"Passage 1: Dashboards and Decisions\\n\\nPublic dashboards can make complex information easier to examine, but visibility does not automatically produce understanding. A chart may be accurate and still mislead if its scale hides variation or if a headline ignores uncertainty. Good dashboards therefore explain where data came from, when they were updated and what they cannot show. They also allow users to compare like with like. The aim is not to remove judgement from decision-making; it is to give judgement a clearer foundation.\\n\\nQuestion: According to the author, data should:\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"eliminate human judgement completely\",\"hi\":\"eliminate human judgement completely\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"support informed judgement rather than replace it\",\"hi\":\"support informed judgement rather than replace it\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"be hidden until uncertainty disappears\",\"hi\":\"be hidden until uncertainty disappears\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"be reduced to a single headline\",\"hi\":\"be reduced to a single headline\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Comprehension Passage\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"bf2acbd7-6609-4748-8d05-31da681300ea\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Passage 3: Decision Fatigue\\n\\nPeople often assume that more choice always improves a decision. In practice, a long series of minor choices can consume attention needed for an important one. This does not mean that choice is undesirable. It suggests that routine decisions should be simplified where possible. A prepared checklist, a fixed time for recurring tasks or a clear default can reduce mental effort without removing meaningful control. The best simplification preserves the decisions that genuinely require thought.\\n\\nQuestion: Why can many minor choices be harmful?\",\"hi\":\"Passage 3: Decision Fatigue\\n\\nPeople often assume that more choice always improves a decision. In practice, a long series of minor choices can consume attention needed for an important one. This does not mean that choice is undesirable. It suggests that routine decisions should be simplified where possible. A prepared checklist, a fixed time for recurring tasks or a clear default can reduce mental effort without removing meaningful control. The best simplification preserves the decisions that genuinely require thought.\\n\\nQuestion: Why can many minor choices be harmful?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"They can use attention needed for more important decisions.\",\"hi\":\"They can use attention needed for more important decisions.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"They permanently remove all personal control.\",\"hi\":\"They permanently remove all personal control.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"They make checklists impossible to use.\",\"hi\":\"They make checklists impossible to use.\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"They ensure that every choice is meaningful.\",\"hi\":\"They ensure that every choice is meaningful.\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Comprehension Passage\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"b2844729-2d31-4c94-9889-f016d832709a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Passage 4: Communicating Scientific Uncertainty\\n\\nUncertainty in a scientific estimate is not evidence that the estimate is useless. It describes the range within which available evidence supports a conclusion. Problems arise when uncertainty is either hidden or exaggerated. Hiding it creates false confidence; exaggerating it can make well-supported findings appear arbitrary. Clear communication states what is known, what remains uncertain and whether new evidence is likely to change the conclusion substantially.\\n\\nQuestion: How can exaggerating uncertainty distort understanding?\",\"hi\":\"Passage 4: Communicating Scientific Uncertainty\\n\\nUncertainty in a scientific estimate is not evidence that the estimate is useless. It describes the range within which available evidence supports a conclusion. Problems arise when uncertainty is either hidden or exaggerated. Hiding it creates false confidence; exaggerating it can make well-supported findings appear arbitrary. Clear communication states what is known, what remains uncertain and whether new evidence is likely to change the conclusion substantially.\\n\\nQuestion: How can exaggerating uncertainty distort understanding?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It can make strong findings seem arbitrary.\",\"hi\":\"It can make strong findings seem arbitrary.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It removes the need for communication.\",\"hi\":\"It removes the need for communication.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It turns estimates into exact facts.\",\"hi\":\"It turns estimates into exact facts.\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It proves that evidence is false.\",\"hi\":\"It proves that evidence is false.\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Compre